{
    "series_title": "The Heart-Hum",
    "series_slug": "bob-emily",
    "series_description": "A heartfelt story of fifteen-year-old Emily and her wheelchair-using cousin Bob, who build an unbreakable bond and a private language called 'The Heart-Hum' to protect each other from a chaotic world.",
    "series_description_long": "---\ntitle: \"Bob Emily\"\n---\nAfter her father's tragic passing, fifteen-year-old Emily\u2014a towering and athletic teenager\u2014finds sanctuary with her aunt and uncle, legally escaping her estranged, conspiracy-obsessed mother. In this new home, she solidifies her bond with her cousin, Bob, a young wheelchair user who shares her profound need for security. \n\nCommunicating through their own private, multi-modal language of sounds and gestures they call \"The Heart-Hum,\" the two become inseparable anchors for each other. From battling sovereign-citizen legal terror in the courtroom to riding the Blue Line bus to Bluewater High, Bob and Emily prove that the strongest fortresses aren't built with walls, but with unconditional understanding, shared resilience, and an unbreakable family bond.",
